# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 1: Map classical inputs to a quantum problem {#step-1-map-classical-inputs-to-a-quantum-problem}"
msgstr "Hakbang 1: I-map ang mga klasikal na input sa isang quantum problem {#step-1-map-classical-inputs-to-a-quantum-problem}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Define $Li_2S$ geometries in dictionary format for different Li-S bond distances to calculate the PES curve. These geometries are optimized using B3LYP/631g calculations.\n"
msgstr "Tukuyin ang mga $Li_2S$ geometry sa dictionary format para sa iba't ibang Li-S bond distance upang kalkulahin ang PES curve. Ang mga geometry na ito ay na-optimize gamit ang mga kalkulasyon ng B3LYP/631g.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The HI-VQE calculations use the options defined in the following cell. With the STO-3G basis, $Li_2S$ has 19 spatial orbitals and 22 electrons. To run the (10o,12e) case with HI-VQE, define 10 active orbitals and freeze the five lowest orbitals, which leaves 12 active electrons. At each iteration, 100 shots are used to sample the electron configurations generated by the ExcitationPreserving quantum circuit (`epa`) with `circular` entanglement and two repetitions (`reps`). The maximum number of iterations is set to 30, which allows enough iterations for the energy to converge.\n"
msgstr "Ginagamit ng mga HI-VQE calculation ang mga option na tinukoy sa sumusunod na cell. Sa STO-3G basis, ang $Li_2S$ ay may 19 spatial orbital at 22 elektron. Para patakbuhin ang (10o,12e) case gamit ang HI-VQE, tukuyin ang 10 active orbital at i-freeze ang limang pinakamababang orbital, na nag-iiwan ng 12 active electron. Sa bawat iteration, 100 shot ang ginagamit para mag-sample ng mga electron configuration na nabuo ng ExcitationPreserving quantum circuit (`epa`) na may `circular` entanglement at dalawang repetition (`reps`). Nakatakda sa 30 ang maximum na bilang ng mga iteration, na nagbibigay ng sapat na iteration para mag-converge ang energy.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Steps 2 and 3: Optimize problem for quantum hardware execution and execute using the HI-VQE Chemistry function {#steps-2-and-3-optimize-problem-for-quantum-hardware-execution-and-execute-using-the-hi-vqe-chemistry-function}"
msgstr "Hakbang 2 at 3: I-optimize ang problema para sa quantum hardware execution at isagawa gamit ang HI-VQE Chemistry function {#steps-2-and-3-optimize-problem-for-quantum-hardware-execution-and-execute-using-the-hi-vqe-chemistry-function}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Set up a `for` loop that submits an HI-VQE job for each geometry, with the options defined previously. In this tutorial, you submit six geometries and retrieve the results after all jobs complete. In the main function run, define `max_states` to control the maximum size of the subspace matrix, and `max_expansion_states` to control how many states classical CI expansion methods can generate per iteration. The function job IDs are stored in a dictionary under each geometry label, so that you can track and process the output.\n"
"These geometries need 20 qubits and run with `max_states=40000`, so the calculator gives `M`. They share their active space and `max_states`, so the size is calculated once.\n"
msgstr ""
"Mag-set up ng `for` loop na nagsusumite ng HI-VQE job para sa bawat geometry, gamit ang mga option na tinukoy kanina. Sa tutorial na ito, magsusumite ka ng anim na geometry at kukunin ang mga resulta kapag nakumpleto na ang lahat ng job. Sa main function run, tukuyin ang `max_states` para kontrolin ang maximum na laki ng subspace matrix, at ang `max_expansion_states` para kontrolin kung ilang state ang kayang buuin ng mga classical CI expansion method bawat iteration. Iniimbak ang mga function job ID sa isang dictionary sa ilalim ng bawat geometry label, para masubaybayan at maproseso mo ang output.\n"
"Nangangailangan ng 20 qubit ang mga geometry na ito at tumatakbo sa `max_states=40000`, kaya `M` ang ibinibigay ng calculator. Pareho ang active space at `max_states` nila, kaya isang beses lang kinakalkula ang laki.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
