#, no-wrap
msgid "[Check](/guides/functions-get-started#check-job-status) whether the jobs are still running or have completed.\n"
msgstr "[Suriin](/guides/functions-get-started#check-job-status) kung tumatakbo pa ang mga job o nakumpleto na.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "After all jobs complete, [retrieve](/guides/functions-get-started#retrieve-results) the calculation results.\n"
msgstr "Kapag nakumpleto na ang lahat ng job, [kunin](/guides/functions-get-started#retrieve-results) ang mga resulta ng calculation.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The results file for each of the calculations can be downloaded into the current directory, under its own name, with `catalog.file_download()`. See [Manage files across runs](/guides/manage-files-across-managed-workflows) for how files are moved to and from a function. These files contain `\"states\"`, `\"eigenvector\"`, `\"energy_history\"`, `\"final_energy\"`, and `\"final_energy_variance\"`.\n"
msgstr "Maaaring i-download ang results file ng bawat calculation sa kasalukuyang directory, sa sarili nitong pangalan, gamit ang `catalog.file_download()`. Tingnan ang [Manage files across runs](/guides/manage-files-across-managed-workflows) para malaman kung paano inililipat ang mga file papunta at mula sa isang function. Naglalaman ang mga file na ito ng `\"states\"`, `\"eigenvector\"`, `\"energy_history\"`, `\"final_energy\"`, at `\"final_energy_variance\"`.\n"

